unim (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Sticky Keys combinations (Ctrl/Alt/Shift + key) intermittently losing
    the modifier on GNOME Wayland: keys the input method will not consume are
    now passed straight through instead of being re-injected, so GNOME's
    Sticky Keys latch survives. Shift+Home / Shift+arrow selection included.
  * Restore rpm packaging: stop rpmbuild's MAKEFLAGS separator from breaking
    the jemalloc build, and request Qt6::GuiPrivate explicitly so Qt 6.8+
    (Fedora 43) configures. 0.4.0 shipped without any rpm.

 -- Seo Kihyun <from104@gmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0900

unim (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First public GitHub release: one-liner installer (install.sh) and
    release CI publishing 11 .deb packages + SHA256SUMS.
  * Auto-English triggers accept Ctrl/Alt/Super combos (e.g. key:Ctrl+B);
    matched keys still pass through to the app (tmux prefix safe).
  * Korean/English toggle beep on Linux (880/440 Hz).
  * Slint settings app (unim-settings) is now the default settings UI on
    Linux; all launchers unified; layouts enumerated from ProfileRegistry.
  * Word-unit input gate: terminals and non-word frontends auto-demote,
    with [WordGate] verdict logging.
  * Super/Meta modifier bit alignment fixed in GTK3/4 and Qt5/6 IMs.
  * Composition fixes on the XIM, Qt and GNOME Wayland paths: clicking while
    composing no longer commits at the click position, the character after a
    commit is no longer one keystroke late, and Enter during composition no
    longer puts the line break before the character.
  * Password-field protection is no longer inert on GNOME Wayland.

 -- Seo Kihyun <from104@gmail.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:30:00 +0900

unim (0.3.63-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * GTK4 settings dialog renamed: unim-settings -> unim-settings-gtk.
  * New package unim-settings: cross-platform Slint settings app with
    first-run wizard; per-login autostart gate (--first-run-if-needed)
    via /etc/xdg/autostart. Re-run manually: unim-settings --first-run.
  * unim-keymap-studio / unim-typing-practice now actually ship their
    binaries, desktop entries, icons and man pages.
  * unim-common now recommends fonts-noto-cjk.
  * Wizard sets the default input method in-process via im-config -n.

