unim (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.3.0.
  * Ahnmatae (안마태 2003) keyboard built-in (`ko_3bul_anmatae`): first
    moachigi (chord-based) Korean layout in UNIM. Three-beol layout with
    fixed cho/jung/jong regions, 9 cho / 15 jung / 20 jong combinations.
    Archaic jamo positions (W/T/G/J/B/N upper) remapped to Korean
    typography symbols (`"` `"` `'` `'` `·` `…`); archaic codepoints
    anywhere in the profile trigger LoadError::ArchaicJamoNotSupported.
  * Layout profile v3 schema (schema_version: 3): single new top-level
    field `supports_moachigi: bool` marks the layout as chord-capable.
    Bidirectional combine and chord window settings live in the user
    config (`~/.config/unim/config.yaml`), not in the keymap JSON.
  * Moachigi chord engine (`src/input_engine/chord_buffer.rs`):
    single-window chord accumulator. First jamo starts an N-ms tokio
    timer; jamo arriving within the window are buffered. On expiry:
    1 jamo → normal sequential processing; 2+ jamo → region-classified
    chord compose with bidirectional combine. Default OFF (opt-in).
  * GTK settings dialog — Moachigi group: toggle row ("동시 입력 자모
    역순 결합") and slider row ("동시 입력 시간 (ms)", 10–100 ms).
    Group is shown only when the selected layout has
    supports_moachigi=true.
  * `HangulComposer3BulMoachigi` separate composer removed; moachigi
    logic is now handled entirely within `HangulComposer3Bul` via the
    `chord_buffer` layer in `InputEngine`. No user-visible behavior
    change.
  * Layout profile v0 schema is no longer supported (legacy JSON files
    without v1 markers are rejected with LoadError::UnsupportedSchema).
  * Packaging: consolidate unim-indicator, unim-settings and
    unim-popup-service into a single unim-desktop bundle (the three
    GTK4 UI processes always ship together on non-GNOME desktops);
    unim-gnome now depends on unim-desktop. Add unim-keymap-studio and
    unim-typing-practice to the `unim` meta-package.

 -- Seo Kihyun <from104@gmail.com>  Tue, 05 May 2026 16:30:00 +0900

unim (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.2.0.
  * Layout Profile v1: built-in keyboard layouts now self-contained v1 JSON
    profiles with user-profile hot reload, inherits chain, rule sets, and
    GUI/CLI integration. New built-in `ko_3bul_qwerty` (10 built-ins total).
  * `KoreanLayout`/`EnglishLayout` enums removed; layout fields now profile
    name strings with backward-compat serde shims for existing config.yaml
    and typefix-blacklist.yaml entries.
  * AutoTypeFix rollback-learned blacklist suppression with Tentative /
    Confirmed / Inactive states, mtime hot reload, and GUI "억제 단어"
    management page (Confirm / Deactivate / Remove / Reactivate).
  * AutoTypeFix reverse-direction gate relaxed to BS-OR-switch, suppression
    key bug fixed, registration moved to retrigger moment.
  * Hanja popup: 9x9 expanded grid mode with Period toggle (GTK Standalone
    + GTK IM + Qt IM + XIM); hanja bookmark UI (Space toggle) across all
    frontends with live HanjaBookmarkChanged signal.
  * Emoji popup (Super+.) with category tabs, search, and MRU favorites
    (GTK + GNOME extension).
  * IME fixes: English-mode Space committed via direct-commit; FocusOut no
    longer emits duplicate CommitText.
  * `tentative_expiry_days` renamed to `tentative_expiry_hours` (1..=12).

 -- Seo Kihyun <from104@gmail.com>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0900

unim (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Modular Korean Input Method Engine written in Rust:
    - Core daemon (unim-daemon) with D-Bus session activation.
    - XIM and Wayland protocol servers (Wayland with
      zwp_input_popup_surface_v2 hanja/special-character popup).
    - C-API library (libunim_capi) and unified CLI tool (unim-cli,
      with a `config` subcommand for settings management).
    - GTK3 and GTK4 input method modules.
    - Qt5 and Qt6 platform input context plugins.
    - GTK4/libadwaita settings GUI (unim-gui-gtk).
    - Qt6/cxx-qt alternative GUI (unim-gui-qt).
    - im-config integration.
  * Supports 2-bul and 3-bul Hangul layouts, automatic Korean/English
    typo correction (TypeFix), Hanja conversion, special-character /
    emoji search and per-application input mode rules.
  * Nine binary packages let users pick the pieces they need:
    - unim-common  : core engine, daemon, CLI, shared library
    - unim-im-gtk  : GTK3 + GTK4 IM modules
    - unim-im-qt   : Qt5 + Qt6 platform input context plugins
    - unim-xim     : X11 XIM protocol frontend
    - unim-wayland : Wayland input-method frontend
    - unim-gui-gtk : GTK4/libadwaita settings GUI + tray
    - unim-gui-qt  : Qt6/cxx-qt settings GUI + tray (alternative)
    - unim-gnome   : GNOME Shell extension
    - unim         : meta-package pulling in everything

 -- from104 <from104@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0900
